From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:23:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/45] serial: 8250_ingenic: Support RS-485

Ingenic boards put half-duplex RS-485 transceivers on their UARTs, the
Flashforge Adventurer 5X its filament changer, with the transceiver's
driver enable on a GPIO. Use the 8250 core's software RS-485 support,
which drives RTS (rts-gpios through mctrl_gpio) around each transmission.

The UART raises no interrupt once its shift register is empty, only when
the FIFO is (THRE): set UART_CAP_NOTEMT so that the driver enable is
released one frame after the FIFO empties, not with the last byte still
being sent.
---
 drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_ingenic.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_ingenic.c b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_ingenic.c
index fbde19d31..7e37f21ee 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_ingenic.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_ingenic.c
@@ -411,7 +411,12 @@ static int ingenic_uart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	uart.port.serial_in = ingenic_uart_serial_in;
 	uart.port.dev = &pdev->dev;
 	uart.tx_loadsz = cdata->tx_loadsz;
-	uart.capabilities = UART_CAP_FIFO | UART_CAP_RTOIE;
+	/* No interrupt when the transmitter is empty, only the FIFO (THRE) */
+	uart.capabilities = UART_CAP_FIFO | UART_CAP_RTOIE | UART_CAP_NOTEMT;
+	uart.port.rs485_config = serial8250_em485_config;
+	uart.port.rs485_supported = serial8250_em485_supported;
+	uart.rs485_start_tx = serial8250_em485_start_tx;
+	uart.rs485_stop_tx = serial8250_em485_stop_tx;
 
 	err = uart_read_port_properties(&uart.port);
 	if (err)
